<p>Israel and the United States launched joint strikes on Iran. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said the campaign would expand to “thousands more targets,” and urged Iranians to unite against what he called a “terror regime”. Several outlets reported that Iran’s supreme leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, was killed; one outlet quoted President Donald Trump as calling that report “correct”. In Israel, opposition figures including Yair Lapid backed the operation publicly and, in some cases, called for regime change. Le Monde described a broader national-unity mood ahead of Israel’s October parliamentary elections. The escalation also disrupted flights and prompted fresh travel warnings as governments and airlines weighed security risks across the region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/on6aIZYAWIaKsbYgOLHvKrB7kGieuqotKJLmFC2XfegnVdySHbNOajueFiY4EfI3YjSVMTbfXr2JtVicOKz-i1ixjXAgeZ0U55dkOMnG-Efw4leI6xE7reEkV1E0af3I4ScZeWCZaiDqqabpqAgn06lph0wexlwK08moQFZMBfny7F05jA' alt='Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu delivers a recorded statement from Jerusalem on February 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Australia and intelligence facilities: Penny Wong said Australia was not told in advance of the strikes, and she declined to say whether Australian-linked facilities such as Pine Gap were used.</li><li>Domestic dissent: A Labor group criticised the Australian government’s stance as “sycophantic capitulation to militarism,” underscoring political disagreement over how Canberra should respond.</li><li>Security meeting: After the strikes, Australia convened a snap meeting of its national security committee involving Prime Minister Anthony Albanese, according to Michael West Media.</li><li>Expanded travel guidance: Smartraveller reiterated “do not travel” advice for Iran, Iraq, Syria and Yemen, and said Australians should reconsider the need to travel to Jordan. It also updated warnings for major regional hubs such as Doha and Dubai.</li><li>Israel’s internal mood: Le Monde described a national-unity dynamic in which Netanyahu’s opponents voiced support, and public opinion was “ready for a new offensive”.</li></ul><blockquote>This is your time to join forces, - Benjamin Netanyahu</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Benjamin Netanyahu (Israel): Netanyahu said Israel would hit “thousands more targets” and argued the operation could create conditions for Iranians to “free themselves from the chains of tyranny”. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-this-is-your-time-to-join-forces-netanyahu-says-to-iranians-after-u-s-israel-attack'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Yair Lapid (Israeli opposition): Lapid said he backed Netanyahu’s decision to strike Iran and called for regime change, describing the campaign as a “just war against evil”. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israeli-opposition-leader-lapid-backs-strikes-on-iran-calls-for-regime-change'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Penny Wong (Australia): Wong backed Israel and the US while saying it was for Australia’s allies to explain the “legal basis” for the attacks, and she did not say whether the Pine Gap facility was used. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/01/penny-wong-backs-israeli-and-us-strikes-on-iran-as-labor-group-decries-sycophantic-capitulation-to-militarism'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/28/israel-rallies-in-national-unity-to-support-attack-on-iran_6750965_4.html'>Israel rallies in national unity to support attack on Iran</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/mar/01/australia-news-live-sunday-iran-illegal-war-reaction-labor-coalition'>Flights from Australia to Middle East cancelled – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/aussie-leaders-back-siege-on-illegitimate-iran-regime/'>Aussie leaders back siege on ‘illegitimate’ Iran regime</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israeli-opposition-leader-lapid-backs-strikes-on-iran-calls-for-regime-change'>Israeli opposition leader Lapid backs strikes on Iran, calls for regime change</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-this-is-your-time-to-join-forces-netanyahu-says-to-iranians-after-u-s-israel-attack'>WATCH: &#x27;This is your time to join forces,&#x27; Netanyahu says to Iranians after U.S.-Israel attack</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>